            "review_title": "Review at Mana Restaurant - Hai Ba Trung D.1",
            "review_text": "Rich7075\nSan Francisco, California415 contributions\n0\nJust an average meal\nFeb 2025 • Couples\nMy wife and I had lunch here for our first meal in HCM. The menu was posted in front of the restaurant and we saw that it was in English. As we were perusing the menu a server came out to greet us. That was enough for us to decide to give it a try.\n\nIt was pretty much empty but for a couple of diners in the back, but then it was after regular lunchtime around 2:00pm. We both ordered the Bun Cha (grilled pork and noodles) and a side order of Spring Rolls. Our order came out pretty quick and everything looked good. \n\nHowever, we were both a little underwhelmed by the taste. It was satisfactory but the meat was tough and the spring rolls did not taste as fresh as we’re expecting. Maybe because it was kind of later in the afternoon or maybe because coming from California we’ve had some very good Vietnamese food. The service was friendly and the interior was clean and inviting. For us it just didn’t have the “Wow” factor we were expecting.\nRead more\nWritten March 16, 2025",
